/** @page authority Which document is authoritative

  Three places describe this project, and they are not equal:

  - **Behaviour** is specified in `openspec/specs/` - one file per capability, each a set of requirements with
    scenarios. When something must be true, that is where it is written, and it is what a change is measured
    against.
  - **Rationale** is in `docs/design/` - why the design is shaped the way it is, what was considered and rejected,
    and how the pieces fit. It explains the specifications; it does not define behaviour.
  - **Work** is on the board in `docs/design/TODO.md`, with task ids the code cites in `TODO(ID)` comments.

  If this site and a specification disagree, the specification is right and the site has a bug. Requirements are
  never restated here: a restated requirement is a requirement with two versions.

  Running it: `docs/design/09-operations.md`. Why it is shaped this way: `docs/direction.md`.
*/

/** @page modules The modules

  Dependencies only ever point leftward: a module may include the ones before it and no others. `match` and
  `flow` have no dependencies at all.

  | Module | What it owns | Contract |
  |---|---|---|
  | core | records, canonical bytes, hashing and signing seams, keystore | `openspec/specs/core/record-integrity` |
  | store | the persistence seam (memory, SQLite) and fork evidence | `openspec/specs/store/log-store` |
  | log | writer-side chaining, replica verification, static verification | `openspec/specs/log/replicated-log` |
  | proto | the binary wire format and its total decoder | `openspec/specs/proto/wire-format` |
  | net | the transport contract, the ZeroMQ transport, peer pinning, simulation | `openspec/specs/net/transport` |
  | node | the single-threaded state machine wiring everything together | `openspec/specs/node/node-runtime` |
  | flow | credit control | `openspec/specs/flow/credit-control` |
  | match | channel pattern matching | `openspec/specs/match/channel-patterns` |
  | jobs | calling a service by name over logs | `openspec/specs/jobs/service-calls` |
  | daemon | `mosaicd`: ZPL configuration, lifecycle, discovery | `openspec/specs/daemon/mosaicd` |

  Each module's own README sits next to its headers - `include/mosaic/<module>/README.md` - and is the page to read
  before changing it.
*/
